On 11/19/07, Chris Capel <pdf23ds@gmail.com> wrote:
> The morphology kicks out "masytcusets" as an invalid cmene. Is this
> correct? (Changing it to "masytcUsetys" makes it parse.) If so, I'm
> gonna try to figure out how to make a comprehensible error message for
> it. Not sure it's possible to make it comprehensible to someone (like
> me) who doesn't know the morphology in some detail, though.

Right, that's because of the final "ts". The current version is not very
happy with final consonant clusters. This is one of the points that are not
at all settled, and probably the official version will end up being
more lenient.
You might be surprized at some of the vowel clusters that get rejected too.

> On a related note, are the production names in the grammar/morphology
> going to get some english-language description at any point in the
> future, so that people have some reference to the meaning of the
> various productions without having to read the grammar? I ask this
> because I'm including some of the production names in LojGloss, but
> many of them don't really have any meaning outside of the grammar
> itself.

I tried to make the rule names in the morphology as self-descriptive
as I could, but I'm sure there's room for improvement.

mu'o mi'e xorxes


